WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:01.719
Oh, snap.

00:00:01.719 --> 00:00:05.419
It looks like Iron Man will be chasing a little
golden man after all.

00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:09.660
Just a month after Disney bosses felt the
wrath of Iron Man fans for not including actor

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.750
Robert Downey Jr. as part of Avengers: Endgame's
Oscars campaign, the Mouse House has officially

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:15.910
changed course.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.550
Disney, which owns Marvel Studios, has now
updated Endgame's "for your consideration"

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.449
page to include Downey Jr.'s name in the Best
Supporting Actor category.

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:25.449
But that's not all.

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:29.689
The Iron Man actor is actually joined in that
category by a veritable who's who of Marvel

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:34.680
Cinematic Universe stalwarts - including Chris
Evans, Mark Ruffalo, Chris Hemsworth, Jeremy

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.690
Renner, Don Cheadle, Josh Brolin and Paul
Rudd on the actor side.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:43.300
Disney is also now pushing Scarlett Johansson,
Gwyneth Paltrow, Zoe Saldana, Karen Gillan

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.280
and Brie Larson in the Best Supporting Actress
race.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.450
That's so many actors, it kind of makes you
feel bad for the people who got left out.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.770
This news comes after what's been a surprisingly
tumultuous month for Disney with regards to

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:57.260
Avengers: Endgame's Academy Awards campaign.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.760
MCU fans reacted with shock that the company
had initially chosen not to push Robert Downey

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.770
Jr. - whom many believed was more than deserving
of an Oscars nomination - or any of the Endgame

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.910
cast in the chase for awards season glory.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:13.220
That decision was even more surprising given
that Disney's original "for your consideration"

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.690
announcement for Endgame included planned
campaigns for Best Picture and Best Director,

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.360
not to mention virtually every technical category.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.950
It now appears that Disney brass may have
simply been figuring out the logistics of

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:28.760
which actors to slot into what category for
Downey Jr. and his MCU teammates.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.710
Fittingly, RDJ will now stand alongside his
fellow Avengers as they attempt to charge

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.960
the Oscars and net the MCU its first acting
statue.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.270
Though an Oscar win is far from guaranteed
for any of the Avengers: Endgame cast, Downey

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:43.369
Jr. in particular seems to have the odds in
his favor.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:47.369
After all, Downey Jr. is seen by most Marvel
fans as the founding father of Disney and

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:52.200
Marvel's superhero franchise machine, with
2008's Iron Man marking the film that blasted

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.799
the MCU into action.

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:57.980
The years since have seen RDJ appear as the
brash-but-brilliant billionaire Tony Stark

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:02.900
in nine more Marvel films - including his
uncredited cameo in The Incredible Hulk - and

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:07.299
that continued presence essentially made Downey
Jr. the face of the MCU over its first three

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:08.299
phases.

00:02:08.299 --> 00:02:11.130
"You know, I hate to say 'I told you so,'
General, but that super soldier program was

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.960
put on ice for a reason.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.020
I've always felt that hardware was much more
reliable."

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:21.319
With the actor's time in the MCU officially
at an end after his tearful Avengers: Endgame

00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:25.740
goodbye, any awards season love for Downey
Jr. would be the culmination of over a decade's

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.590
worth of work inhabiting what has more often
than not been the MCU's most complex character.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.510
But while Iron Man fans will almost certainly
be over the moon that Downey Jr. may have

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.580
a chance to take a bow with a golden statue
in his hand on Hollywood's biggest night,

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.750
the man himself may not be quite as excited
at this unexpected turn of events.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.730
After that initial "no Oscar campaign for
RDJ's Iron Man" news broke, the actor used

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.630
an appearance on The Howard Stern Show to
address the supposed snub, telling the world

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.490
that he wasn't really into an Oscar campaign
for his work in Avengers: Endgame to begin

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:56.490
with.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:57.490
He explained to Stern:

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:00.030
"There was some talk about it and I said,
'Let's not.'"

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.000
Like it or not, Downey Jr.'s iron hat has
officially been tossed into the awards season

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.450
ring for what's certain to be an intriguing
supporting actor battle.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.770
But even if it remains unlikely in the grand
scheme that RDJ will take home a statue at

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:16.470
the 2020 Oscars, the idea that his iconic
work as the MCU's top dog hasn't earned him

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:20.030
a spot in the conversation until now is pretty
absurd.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:24.360
All that being said, if there's a second Avengers:
Endgame actor worthy of generating serious

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.060
Oscars buzz, it's Chris Hemsworth.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.150
After toiling away in a pair of underwhelming
Thor movies, the God of Thunder finally found

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.350
his mojo in Taika Waititi's Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:38.190
But nothing we'd seen of Hemsworth's Thor
could've prepared us for the actor's heart-wrenching

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.239
work in Endgame.

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:45.260
"I'm still worthy…"

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:54.159
While RDJ's teaful farewell proved a crowning
achievement of the MCU, watching Hemsworth's

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:58.069
"Fat Thor" work through the emotional carnage
of his once-privileged life was often the

00:03:58.069 --> 00:03:59.849
most intriguing element of Endgame.

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:04.370
So yeah, if the Academy is preparing to show
Downey Jr. some love, it'd be nice to see

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.599
Hemsworth sharing in that adoration.

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:10.379
For now, we should probably just be happy
that Robert Downey Jr. is officially part

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:11.710
of the awards season chatter.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.620
Here's hoping the Academy loves him 3,000.

